" ============================================================
"  IdeaVim config — mirroring Doom Emacs / Nordic key layout
"  j=Left  k=Down  l=Up  ø=Right  (instead of h/j/k/l)
" ============================================================

" ── Plugins ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
set surround          " vim-surround: cs, ds, ys
set commentary        " gc to comment
set highlightedyank   " briefly highlight yanked text
set NERDTree          " file tree (optional, open with <Space>op style)
set ideajoin          " smart J join using IDE logic
set ideamarks         " sync vim marks with IDE bookmarks

" ── Core settings ───────────────────────────────────────────
set number            " line numbers on
set relativenumber    " relative by default (matches display-line-numbers-type 'relative)
set scrolloff=5
set incsearch
set ignorecase
set smartcase
set showmode
set clipboard=unnamedplus " use the system clipboard by default

" ── Nordic movement: j=← k=↓ l=↑ ø=→ ──────────────────────
" Normal / Visual / Operator-pending
noremap j h
noremap k j
noremap l k
noremap ø l

" Keep the original h/j/k/l targets reachable (shifted one step)
" h is repurposed below — original h (move left) is now j

" ── Window navigation: C-j/k/l/ø ───────────────────────────
nnoremap <C-j> <C-w>h
nnoremap <C-k> <C-w>j
nnoremap <C-l> <C-w>k
nnoremap <C-ø> <C-w>l                     " doesn't work, set it manually
nnoremap <C-M-j> :action PreviousTab<CR>
nnoremap <C-M-ø> :action NextTab<CR>      " doesn't work, set it manually

" ── h: cycle line number modes ──────────────────────────────
" relative → absolute → none → relative …
" IdeaVim doesn't have a scripting engine to toggle state, so we
" map h to the IDE action that toggles relative numbers on/off.
" Two presses cycle: relative → off, press again → absolute, etc.
" Best approximation: map h to toggle relative numbers via IDE.
nnoremap h :set relativenumber!<CR>

" ── Buffer switching: [b / ]b ──────────────────────────────
nnoremap [b :action Back<CR>
nnoremap ]b :action Forward<CR>

" ── Jumping within buffer ──────────────────────────────
nnoremap [e :action GotoPreviousError<CR>
nnoremap ]e :action GotoNextError<CR>

" ── Jump history: C-o / C-i ─────────────────────────────────
" IdeaVim preserves Vim's native <C-o> (jump back) and <C-i> (jump
" forward) by default. These move through the full jump list, which
" spans cursor positions both within the current file and across
" files — exactly like Emacs' better-jumper / evil-jump-backward.
" No remapping needed; just don't override them elsewhere.
" (The previous C-o = PreviousTab / C-i = NextTab IDE defaults are
"  intentionally left unmapped here so jump history takes priority.)

" ── Go-to-definition in other window (gw) ───────────────────
" IdeaVim equivalent: open definition in a split
nnoremap gw :action GotoDeclaration<CR>
" (use <C-w>gd or the action below to get "other window" behaviour)
nnoremap gW :action QuickImplementations<CR>

" ── Code navigation / LSP-equivalents ───────────────────────
nnoremap gr :action FindUsages<CR>
nnoremap gi :action GotoImplementation<CR>
nnoremap gD :action GotoTypeDeclaration<CR>
nnoremap K  :action QuickJavaDoc<CR>

" ── Structural editing (smartparens → IdeaVim) ──────────────
" M-j  sp-forward-barf-sexp   → unwrap/barf forward
" M-ø  sp-forward-slurp-sexp  → slurp forward
" M-k  sp-backward-slurp-sexp → slurp backward
" M-l  sp-backward-barf-sexp  → barf backward
" IdeaVim has no sexp plugin, so bind to ParEdit-style IDE actions.
" If you install the 'IntelliJ IDEA Community / IdeaVim-EasyMotion'
" or 'Cursive' plugin, replace with their specific actions.
nnoremap <M-j> :action MoveStatementDown<CR>
nnoremap <M-l> :action MoveStatementUp<CR>
vnoremap <M-j> :action MoveStatementDown<CR>
vnoremap <M-l> :action MoveStatementUp<CR>

" ── Format on save (mirrors +format-on-save-enabled-modes) ──
" Enable via IDE: Settings → Tools → Actions on Save → Reformat code
" Nothing to set in .ideavimrc, but noted here for reference.

" ── Leader key (Space, like Doom Emacs SPC) ─────────────────
let mapleader = " "

" File
nnoremap <leader>ff :action GotoFile<CR>
nnoremap <leader>fr :action RecentFiles<CR>
nnoremap <leader>fs :action SaveAll<CR>

" Buffer / Editor
nnoremap <leader>bd :action CloseContent<CR>
nnoremap <leader>bb :action RecentFiles<CR>
nnoremap <leader>bn :action NextTab<CR>
nnoremap <leader>bp :action PreviousTab<CR>

" Search (mirrors SPC s)
nnoremap <leader>sp :action FindInPath<CR>
nnoremap <leader>ss :action GotoSymbol<CR>
nnoremap <leader>sb :action FindInCurrentFile<CR>

" Code (mirrors SPC c)
nnoremap <leader>ca :action ShowIntentionActions<CR>
nnoremap <leader>cr :action RenameElement<CR>
nnoremap <leader>cf :action ReformatCode<CR>
nnoremap <leader>cd :action ShowErrorDescription<CR>

" Git (mirrors SPC g)
nnoremap <leader>gg :action ActivateVersionControlToolWindow<CR>
nnoremap <leader>gb :action Annotate<CR>
nnoremap <leader>gl :action Vcs.ShowTabbedFileHistory<CR>

" Project / Window (mirrors SPC w / SPC p)
nnoremap <leader>wv :action SplitVertically<CR>
nnoremap <C-x>3 :action SplitVertically<CR>
nnoremap <leader>ws :action SplitHorizontally<CR>
nnoremap <C-x>2 :action SplitHorizontally<CR>
nnoremap <leader>wd :action Unsplit<CR>
nnoremap <C-x>1 :action UnsplitAll<CR>
nnoremap <C-x>0 :action CloseContent<CR>
nnoremap <leader>op :action ActivateProjectToolWindow<CR>
nnoremap <leader>ot :action ActivateTerminalToolWindow<CR>
